docs/reviews/backlog-2026-09-02-kimi.md:7:  **3. D1 — the two-point transform is the measured m/z defect, but the −11.7% attribution is not isolated (major).** Confounds the row ignores: (a) the 1/K0 axis differs by construction ("converter-recalibrated 1/K0 vs our rational TIMS calibration", RUNTIME-PLAN line 219), and every IM-denominated gate — `pickIMCluster:im_tolerance_cluster` (`:1694`), `charge:iso_im_tolerance`, `im_weight_sigma` — shifts with it; (b) the reader matches windows by nearest `selected_ion_mz` within 0.05 Da (`MzPeakStreamLoad.h:141-142`) under an m/z axis bowed ~7 ppm — near-boundary windows can mis-match; (c) +2,693 spectra (925,595 vs 922,902) is unexplained in any doc. The D4 workaround dropping the per-window IM band restriction also admits off-band interferents into the corr gates. Correction: root cause → "two-point m/z proven (+7 ppm bow); peptide-loss attribution pending; IM axis uncontrolled." Pre-register step 8's falsifier: exact-calibration mzPeak must recover ≈12,217 peptides with high set overlap vs d2_P1; if it doesn't, the IM axis is implicated.
