patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:1:# SpeXtractor: give OpenMS MassTrace move operations.
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:2:#
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:3:# MassTrace declares a defaulted destructor, copy constructor and copy assignment, which suppresses
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:4:# the implicit move operations: every std::move of a MassTrace -- in MassTraceDetection's and
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:5:# ElutionPeakDetection's own vector growth and in SpeXtractor's band/split gathering -- was a deep
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:6:# copy of trace_peaks_ (24 B/point) and smoothed_intensities_ (8 B/point). Two defaulted moves make
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:7:# those transfers; the values are bitwise the same, so the output is identical. SpeXtractor
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:8:# static_asserts std::is_nothrow_move_constructible<MassTrace>, so a tree without this patch does
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:9:# not build the tool.
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:10:#
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:11:# Base: OpenMS/OpenMS develop bd4b89555629d68b431b189a4c841efbcc4dfeea (2026-04-24).
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:12:# Apply from the OpenMS tree root: patch -p1 -N < openms-masstrace-move.patch
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:13:--- a/src/openms/include/OpenMS/KERNEL/MassTrace.h
patches/openms-masstrace-move.patch:14:+++ b/src/openms/include/OpenMS/KERNEL/MassTrace.h
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:1:# SpeXtractor: make OpenMS ElutionPeakDetection lock-free for nested parallel callers.
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:2:#
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:3:# detectPeaks(vector) guarded a shared output vector with a PROGRAM-GLOBAL named critical. Called
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:4:# from inside SpeXtractor's per-band trace loop (96 concurrent callers) that one lock serialised the
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:5:# whole tool: 195M context switches, 37% system time. At top level this now collects into
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:6:# per-thread buffers and merges; when already nested it runs serially into the caller's own vector.
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:7:# No output vector is ever shared across threads, so the critical is unnecessary. Numerically
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:8:# identical: verified 1,528,113 spectra / 10,036 peptides identical across two machines.
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:9:#
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:10:# Base: OpenMS/OpenMS develop bd4b89555629d68b431b189a4c841efbcc4dfeea (2026-04-24).
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:11:# Regenerated 2026-09-05 as a UNIFIED diff. The previous version was a headerless NORMAL diff
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:12:# ("328,330c328,334") naming no file at all, so `patch` could not know what to modify and ignored
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:13:# every hunk -- which is why the CI build failed at the patch step.
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:14:# Apply with: patch -p1 -d <OpenMS tree> < this file
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:15:--- a/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/ElutionPeakDetection.cpp
patches/openms-epd-lockfree.patch:16:+++ b/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/ElutionPeakDetection.cpp
patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:1:# SpeXtractor: vendor m/z calibration for the Bruker timsTOF reader.
patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:2:#
patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:3:# Without this the reader converts flight time to m/z with a two-point linear-in-sqrt chord that is
patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:4:# -5 to -11 ppm biased (m/z dependent), costing roughly 6-11% of closed-search peptide
patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:5:# identifications. This uses the vendor's own MzCalibration table from analysis.tdf instead, and
patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:6:# exports BrukerTimsFile::lastMzCalibration() so the emitted file can record which path ran.
